<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">United Belgian States</h1><p class="st-meta">1790 CE – 1790 CE · capital Brussels</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first independent Belgian state, a confederation formed in the Brabant Revolution of 1789–1790 and modelled partly on the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Joseph II</a>'s reforms of courts, church and administration angered the estates of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrian-netherlands">Austrian Netherlands</a>. In 1789 exiles organised an army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breda">Breda</a>, defeated the Austrians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-turnhout-1789">Turnhout</a> in October, and by December drove them from most of the country. On 11 January 1790 the provinces declared independence as the United Belgian States.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation's treaty created a sovereign congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> while leaving each province its old institutions. Power lay with the conservative Statists of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-van-der-noot">Henri van der Noot</a>, who defended traditional privileges and the Church, against the democratic Vonckists of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-francois-vonck">Jean-François Vonck</a>, who were driven into exile. No foreign power recognised the state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Divided and without allies, the United Belgian States collapsed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Leopold II's</a> Austrian army reoccupied the country in December 1790. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrian-netherlands">Austrian Netherlands</a> was restored until the French conquest of 1794.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-belgian-states.jpg" alt="United Belgian States" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_of_Belgium_(1790).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1790 CE – 1790 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brussels</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henri van der Noot, Jean-François Vonck, Jean-André van der Mersch</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United States of Belgium, Belgian Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1790&amp;focus=united-belgian-states" aria-label="United Belgian States on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4779 414 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United Belgian States lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5099 670L5099 670M5099 670L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5099 670h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5099 670h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5099 670h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1790&amp;focus=united-belgian-states">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
